+// RNE modification (see RNE_PATCH.md): Inria-correct EWA splatting.
+//
+// Upstream 0.2.0 used `proj[i][i] * size` as the pixel focal length (2f instead
+// of f), so its 2D covariance was 4x too large; it added a 0.1 low-pass in those
+// doubled units (~0.025 px^2) and drew `exp(-q^2)` with `q` in units of
+// `sqrt(lambda)` of that covariance. Every splat came out sqrt(2) wider than the
+// trained footprint. This version follows the reference rasterizer
+// (Kerbl et al. 2023, diff-gaussian-rasterization):
+// - focal length f = proj[i][i] * size / 2 pixels, with the 1.3 * tan(fov / 2)
+//   clamp of the view-space x/z, y/z in the Jacobian;
+// - +0.3 px^2 low-pass on the 2D covariance diagonal (no Mip-Splatting
+//   opacity compensation);
+// - quad half-axes of 3 sigma along the eigenvectors, `quad_offset` carrying the
+//   offset in sigma units of each axis, so |q|^2 = d^T Sigma^-1 d;
+// - alpha = min(0.99, opacity * exp(-0.5 |q|^2)), discarded below 1/255.
+const max_radius = 3.0;
+const max_extent_px = 1024.0;
+const min_alpha = 1.0 / 255.0;
+const max_alpha = 0.99;
